{
 "kind": "job_benchmark",
 "date": "2026-10-07",
 "scope": "Whole Quick Sim jobs of the 42 single-target production requests (fixtures/mage/prepared-v2/production-*.request.json) at 3000 iterations, the production Quick Sim size, run as the worker would from a bundle once Rust prepares every class: Go as one pinned engine process on the request, Rust as tools/route.py, which now runs one Rust process that prepares the request itself, gates the prepared state and simulates it, and starts the Go exporter only after a preparation refusal.",
 "method": "tools/job_bench.py interleaves the Go job, the routed Rust job and the steps of a routed job on their own (the Go exporter's prepare, Rust's prepare, and the gate with the simulation), three rounds per request; each figure is the median over the rounds. Wall time is measured around each process; CPU time and peak resident set come from wait4 and include every process a job waits for. Overhead is a job's wall time minus the engine's own iteration loop time. The throughput phase runs every routed request's job three times, four jobs at a time, in each engine.",
 "command": "python3 tools/job_bench.py --bundle <scratch>/bundle --output <scratch>/report.json --rounds 3 --iterations 3000 --concurrency 4",
 "source_revision": "a5557db5eccd1dfbd4cf1280c67a451f3ff3c8c4",
